{
  "_readme": [
    "Edit this file to change what Food Lens flags. No code changes needed.",
    "categories: what each kind of ingredient means. Values: non_veg (meat, fish, gelatine...), egg, animal_veg (animal but veg: milk, honey), maybe_non_veg (could be animal: E471, Lab), maybe_egg, maybe_animal_veg (could be animal but still veg, e.g. vitamin D3 - only affects 'vegan').",
    "A product is: Non-veg if any non_veg ingredient; Contains egg if any egg; Unclear if any maybe_non_veg / maybe_egg; Veg if any animal_veg / maybe_animal_veg; otherwise Vegan.",
    "rules.terms: matched case-insensitively against the ingredient text (German and English). '=word' must be a whole word ('=ei' won't match 'Eis'). '^word' must start a word ('^lamm' matches 'Lammkeule' but not 'Flammkuchen'). Plain terms match anywhere, including inside German compound words.",
    "E-numbers are written without spaces ('e441'); 'E 441' and 'E-441' on labels are normalised automatically.",
    "rules.exclude: phrases removed before this rule is checked, to avoid false alarms (e.g. 'fruchtfleisch' is fruit pulp, not meat).",
    "rules.okIfFollowedBy: if one of these words appears within ~45 characters after the match (e.g. 'E471 (pflanzlich)'), the match is ignored."
  ],
  "categories": {
    "meat": "non_veg",
    "fish": "non_veg",
    "gelatin": "non_veg",
    "insect": "non_veg",
    "egg": "egg",
